From: =?UTF-8?q?Do=C4=9Fukan=20Korkmazt=C3=BCrk?= <dkorkmazturk@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 11:31:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 27/38] Return invalid fd on syncobj creation failure

eplWlTimelinePointToSyncFD returns a file descriptor, where negative
values indicate failure. Returning EGL_FALSE from the drmSyncobjCreate
failure path produced integer 0, which is a valid file descriptor and
could be treated as a valid sync fd by callers.

Return -1 instead so a failure would correctly return an invalid fd.
---
 src/wayland/wayland-timeline.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/wayland/wayland-timeline.c b/src/wayland/wayland-timeline.c
index 4b87c30..263554e 100644
--- a/src/wayland/wayland-timeline.c
+++ b/src/wayland/wayland-timeline.c
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@ int eplWlTimelinePointToSyncFD(WlDisplayInstance *inst, WlTimeline *timeline)
                 gbm_device_get_fd(inst->gbmdev),
                 0, &tempobj) != 0)
     {
-        return EGL_FALSE;
+        return -1;
     }
 
     if (inst->platform->priv->drm.SyncobjTransfer(gbm_device_get_fd(inst->gbmdev),
